{
  "about": "Linked Tables (ADR-0049, ticket 16, SH-16) and a table's key (ADR-0049 2026-09-30, ADR-0058, SH-33): the wait, the snapshot, what a copy and a Sheet Document hold, the declaration and its refusals, and a key that repeats. Transcribed from LinkedTableTests.cs.",
  "kind": "sheet",
  "culture": "en-US",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049 (SH-16): the first snapshot replaces the wait everywhere it reached",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Positions[PV])", "B1": "=A1*2"}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1", 21, "FX"]]}, "expect": {"values": {"B1": 42}, "change": {"valueChanges": ["A1", "B1"]}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049 (SH-16): an undeclared table name is #NAME?, and declaring it makes its readers wait",
      "steps": [
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Rates[Mid])"}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#NAME?"}}}},
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Rates", "columns": ["Pair", "Mid"]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}, "change": {"valueChanges": ["A1"]}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049 (SH-16): a new snapshot recalculates only the table's readers and what depends on them",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1001", 100, "Rates"], ["R-4471", 250.5, "FX"], ["R-2002", -50, "Rates"]]}},
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Rates", "columns": ["Pair", "Mid"]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Positions[PV])", "A2": "=A1+1", "A3": "=COUNTA(Rates[Pair])", "A4": "7", "A5": "=A4*2"}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1", 1, "FX"]]}, "expect": {"change": {"recalculated": ["A1", "A2"]}, "values": {"A2": 2}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049 (SH-16): a snapshot replaces the last in one step; no recalculation sees a mix",
      "note": "Both columns come from the same snapshot, so the difference is always 0.",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Book", "columns": ["Long", "Short"]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Book[Long])-SUM(Book[Short])", "A2": "=COUNT(Book[Long])-COUNT(Book[Short])"}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Book", "rows": [[1, 1]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 0, "A2": 0}}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Book", "rows": [[2, 2], [4, 4]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 0, "A2": 0}}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Book", "rows": [[3, 3], [6, 6], [9, 9]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 0, "A2": 0}}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Book", "rows": [[4, 4], [8, 8], [12, 12], [16, 16]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 0, "A2": 0}}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Book", "rows": [[5, 5], [10, 10], [15, 15], [20, 20], [25, 25]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 0, "A2": 0}}},
        {"read": true, "expect": {"workbook": {"linkedTables": [{"name": "Book", "rowCount": 5}]}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049 (SH-16): a copy reaching a waiting cell is refused, and one that does not is not",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "1", "B2": "=SUM(Positions[PV])"}},
        {"copy": {"range": "A1:C3", "as": "reaching"}},
        {"copy": {"range": "A1:A3", "as": "beside"}, "expect": {"copies": {"reaching": {"refusal": "waitingForData", "saying": "B2 is waiting for a Linked Table's data (#GETTING_DATA); a copy would carry a wait that means nothing where it lands.", "text": null, "block": null}, "beside": {"refusal": null}}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0046/0049: a reader moved by an insertion still reads its table",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1001", 100, "Rates"], ["R-4471", 250.5, "FX"], ["R-2002", -50, "Rates"]]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Positions[PV])"}},
        {"do": {"insertRows": [0, 1]}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["x", 9, "y"]]}, "expect": {"change": {"recalculated": ["A2"]}, "values": {"A2": 9}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0048/0049: a Sheet Document holds the Formulas that name a table and its declaration, never its rows",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1001", 100, "Rates"], ["R-4471", 250.5, "FX"], ["R-2002", -50, "Rates"]]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Positions[PV])"}, "expect": {"documentJson": "{\"version\":9,\"culture\":\"en-US\",\"name\":\"Sheet1\",\"linkedTables\":[{\"name\":\"Positions\",\"columns\":[\"Id\",\"PV\",\"Desk\"]}],\"cells\":[{\"at\":\"A1\",\"formula\":\"=SUM(Positions[PV])\"}]}"}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049: opening a document shows #GETTING_DATA for every reader until the first push, never #NAME?",
      "steps": [
        {"declareTable": {"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"]}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-1001", 100, "Rates"], ["R-4471", 250.5, "FX"], ["R-2002", -50, "Rates"]]}},
        {"enter": {"A1": "=SUM(Positions[PV])", "A2": "=IFERROR(XLOOKUP(\"R-4471\",Positions[Id],Positions[PV]),0)", "A3": "=A1+1"}},
        {"reopen": "json", "expect": {"values": {"A1": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}, "A2": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}, "A3": {"error": "#GETTING_DATA"}}, "workbook": {"linkedTables": [{"name": "Positions", "columns": ["Id", "PV", "Desk"], "keyColumns": [], "isWaiting": true, "rowCount": 0}]}}},
        {"pushTable": {"name": "Positions", "rows": [["R-4471", 250.5, "FX"]]}, "expect": {"values": {"A1": 250.5, "A2": 250.5, "A3": 251.5}, "change": {"valueChanges": ["A1", "A2", "A3"]}}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ADR-0049, ADR-0047: a column's name holding @ [ ] # or ' is stored escaped, and the stored text reads back as the same reference, again and again: =SUM(Positions[['@PV]])",
